--   $$s\,a_{\mathrm{target}}\le\sum_j\lambda_j a_j,\qquad s>0,\quad\lambda_j\ge0.$$
--
--   Strictness is recorded explicitly. Coordinate cuts connect the leaves, and separate exact checks validate this proof data. Referenced fragments are ordinary child proof fragments, allowing finite verification to be partitioned without changing the real domain.
-- source:
--   Fujiwara, Gutowski, Ouchi and Wolff, STOC 2027 submission #885, Section 3 equation (2) and its proof, printed p. 8 (PDF p. 9), Section 4 Table 1 and verification, printed pp. 9–11 (PDF pp. 10–12), https://github.com/sigact-stoc/stoc2027/releases/download/papers-1/885.pdf. Certificate family D8; explicit linear-combination proof of a fragment of query (4) or (5).

